            "description": "Registers a new user account in the Express-YouTube API.\n\n- **Method & URL**: `POST {{domain}}/users/register`\n    \n- **Auth**: No authentication required; this is a public sign-up endpoint.\n    \n- **Body type**: `multipart/form-data`\n    \n\n### Request body fields\n\n- `fullName` (string, required): User’s full display name. Example: `Kirtan Gajjar`.\n    \n- `email` (string, required): User’s email address. Must be unique and in valid email format. Example: `kitten@gmail.com`.\n    \n- `password` (string, required): User’s password. The server may enforce minimum length/complexity rules.\n    \n- `username` (string, required): Public username/handle for the account. Must be unique. Example: `kitten`.\n    \n\n### Typical responses\n\n- **201 Created / 200 OK**: User registered successfully. The response usually includes basic user details and/or an auth token depending on server implementation.\n    \n- **400 Bad Request**: Missing or invalid fields (e.g., invalid email format, weak password, missing required fields).\n    \n- **409 Conflict**: Email or username already in use.\n    \n- **500 Internal Server Error**: Unexpected server-side failure while creating the account.\n    \n\nUse this endpoint to create a new user that can later authenticate and interact with the API."
          },
          "response": []
        },
